  "semantic_checks": [
    "Normalization multiplies the actual polynomial family by D^-m S^-|gamma| and evaluates it at the actual block-scaled point (DX,Ss). Its global termwise identity with the original sum is proved, not assumed; positive D,S are explicit where inverses normalize budgets.",
    "The normalized actual coefficient-L1 budget is at most M. The quarter-block inequalities imply the full normalized sup norm is at most 1/4. Thus the coarse total-order estimate is 2^(d+1) M 4^k k! at that exact point.",
    "The block scaling map is an actual complex continuous linear map. It sends each coordinate unit vector to its own block scalar times the same vector, giving exactly |D| or |S| per direction.",
    "The local linear chain lemma obtains an open neighborhood from ContDiffAt and applies the pinned within-set iterated chain rule on that neighborhood. It requires no global smoothness. Normalized actual analyticity supplies the local ContDiffAt premise in the consumer.",
    "The coordinate-word theorem uses the global normalized-function equality to rewrite the original derivative, then the actual local linear chain rule and multilinearity. It retains the full product of individual block factors; it does not replace them by a maximum operator norm.",
    "The fixed multiindex coordinate word is selected from a proved finite exponent-word existence theorem. Its length is the actual sum of exponents, its real product identity holds for every weight, and applying that identity to the weight 2 at one coordinate proves the exact occurrence count by injectivity of powers of 2.",
    "complexMultiindexDeriv is the literal iterated complex Frechet derivative at total order, evaluated on those actual coordinate unit directions. It is not an assumed derivative family or a value supplied by an existence premise.",
    "The factorial inequality k! <= q^k product(alpha_i!) is proved through the finite multinomial expansion at all coordinate values one, with q equal to the actual coordinate count. Empty coordinate sets and k=0 are included in the prerequisite.",
    "For Fin 3 plus Fin d, q=3+d. Combining the coordinate product identity with the proved factorial inequality yields the exact rate 4(3+d) in addition to each separate coefficient rate.",
    "The mixed endpoint for alpha on Fin 3 and beta on Fin d is 2^(d+1) M [4(3+d)D]^|alpha| [4(3+d)S]^|beta| alpha! beta!, on D||X||<=1/4 and S||s||<=1/4. No dimension or factorial factors are suppressed.",
    "The prescribed KS endpoint consumes the actual degree, balance and original per-coefficient inputs via the reviewed data theorem. It uses D=32b^2 and keeps the shifted B amplitude MD; the extra D is not lost.",
    "Constant terms, zero total derivative order, M=0 and d=0 are included. The normalization and prescribed derivative endpoints explicitly require positive rates; zero-rate analytic theorems are separate and not implicitly imported into these derivative statements."
  ],
